WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.548
Start and controls
Take a seat and press Ready. The host starts when everyone is ready. Your cards or dice are at the bottom.

00:00:12.548 --> 00:00:18.848
Follow the turn prompt. Wait for animations to finish; an expired turn is played automatically. Use Return to room after settlement.

00:00:18.848 --> 00:00:34.848
Big Two: empty your hand first
Each player has 13 cards. Follow the player holding the club three throughout this match; other hands show counts only.

00:00:34.848 --> 00:00:44.748
Open with the club three
Click cards, then press Play. Select a single, a pair, or a legal five-card combination; the opening play must include the club three.

00:00:44.748 --> 00:00:52.848
Ranks run from 3 low to 2 high. Tied ranks use clubs, diamonds, hearts, spades in ascending order. Turns run counterclockwise.

00:00:52.848 --> 00:01:03.848
Beat the current play
Check the table combination, select a stronger legal play, then press Play. Click a selected card again or press Clear to change your selection.

00:01:03.848 --> 00:01:12.848
An ordinary response must match the card count and combination type and be stronger. Bombs are the exception.

00:01:12.848 --> 00:01:23.848
Pass and regain the lead
Press Pass to sit out. Watch the pass markers and log: when everyone else has passed, the last player to play leads freely again.

00:01:23.848 --> 00:01:32.848
A pass locks you out for this round. A new round unlocks everyone. You cannot pass on a free lead; no legal response triggers an automatic pass.

00:01:32.848 --> 00:01:44.948
Play five cards together
On a free lead, select five cards forming a full house or another legal combination, then check the type shown on Play. Watch the following five-card comparison.

00:01:44.948 --> 00:01:54.850
Straights and full houses only beat their own type. Four of a kind plus a kicker and straight flushes are bombs; a straight flush beats four of a kind.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:02:05.850
Some groups are not legal plays
Players may save their cards by passing. Finish this round of passes and watch who receives the next free lead.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:14.850
A bare triple, any four-card play, and an ordinary flush are invalid. Straights range from A2345 to 10JQKA; wrapped runs such as JQKA2 are invalid.

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:32.849
Pairs and control of the lead
Watch matching ranks form pairs and beat smaller pairs. Each new free lead lets its owner choose singles, pairs, or five cards again.

00:02:32.849 --> 00:02:57.849
Speed through the rest of the deal
The remaining legal plays and passes run in order at higher speed. Watch hand counts until someone empties their hand normally.

00:02:57.849 --> 00:03:14.834
Big Two: final settlement
Demo W finishes first. The others have 9, 6, and 4 cards left, with no twos remaining.
